{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395587-ventrue-feeding-preferences","id":1395587,"title":"Ventrue Feeding Preferences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-10T06:47:29-07:00","id":1395587,"title":"Ventrue Feeding Preferences","content":"I'm hoping to brainstorm some ideas for Ventrue feeding preferences, hopefully at least a few dozen to choose among.<br /> <br /> I may be running a session with a heavily attended Ventrue meeting soon, and feeding preferences will figure in the plot. Basically, the pcs are ghouls and will be hired for kitchen duty. I'm looking for a wide and varied &quot;shopping list&quot;.<br /> <br /> I know, I know, most Ventrue would handle their own refreshments. The local Prince, however, wants guests to feed in an orderly manner, rather than flooding out into the city to drain it dry. Attendees will provide their preference anonymously. Vessels of appropriate types will all be brought to a party where the guests can hunt, knowing their preference will be available without necessarily revealing their preference. The pcs, however, having researched the vessels, may be able to deduce the preferences.<br /> <br /> Also, what are your thoughts on the parameters of feeding preferences? There is a tremendous range in canon, from <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Tiamat_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">those who feed on half the adult population</a> to <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bobby_Weatherbottom\" target=\"_blank\">those who feed on a single perso</a>n. As an ST, how do you decide which feeding preferences to approve for pcs? What are your thoughts on the etiquette of entertaining Ventrue? Do you run Ventrue preferences being a tightly held secret, hidden-but-discoverable fact, or publicly known? Also, how do you handle Dignitas and feeding preferences? Is there cachet attached to certain preferences, and shame for others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T07:16:58-07:00","id":1395590,"title":"","content":"i'd say given the level of paranoia kindred operate under feeding preferences are greatly held secret. and dignitas is all about image and reputation and in the eyes of kindred all humans are just cattle. if ones preferences is gonna hurt their reputation it's because they did something embracing to get it (like being seen in a shody neighborhood) and not who they drank from. but they keep it hidden anyway because it could be an exploitable weakness.<br /> <br /> as for how limited a PCs presence should be that entirely depends on what you want to do, do you want it to not get in the way of the story, you allow whatever the player wants, but if you want it to be used as a storyhook you should limit it to things you can work with (like a ventrue is limited to drug addicts and his rival finds out so he launches a massive anti-drugs campaign, that sort of thing) so do whatever fits your story the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T09:51:48-07:00","id":1395613,"title":"","content":"all feeding preferences are fine for my pcs. even bullshit like 'only natives of the city we're in'. the caveat is that ventrue get suspicious/jealous of those with wider feeding circles than they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T10:11:52-07:00","id":1395616,"title":"","content":"My ancient Roman Ventrue had the feeding restriction \u201conly people she finds attractive.\u201d Luckily this was a fairly broad range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T10:33:34-07:00","id":1395620,"title":"","content":"The rule I generally use is this: &quot;Your feeding is restricted to one particular type of prey (almost always a type of human). For whatever reason, you cannot tolerate vitae of other types, and you will become very ill if you consume blood of an origin you cannot determine to be within your prey-class (take one health level of damage for each point so consumed). Your prey-class must be described in your character background, and it must be sufficiently restrictive to exclude at least 75% of possible mortal prey.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of dynamic categories -- that is, categories whose membership changes depending on the circumstances.<br /> <br /> I also try very hard not to have something that is keyed to a particular time period or cultural milieu. Vampires who are limited to people who own a Mercedes (to give a painfully bad example) are gonna be up the creek in 200 years when there are no Mercedeses to be had.<br /> <br /> As for types of restrictions, here are a couple from my Ventrue NPCs over the years:<br /> <br /> * Third children<br /> * Pregnant mothers<br /> * The left-handed<br /> * Religious leaders (pastors, priests, rabbis, imams, etc.)<br /> * Those who have taken a human life<br /> * People who make a literary or cultural reference that the vampire recognizes (without prompting)<br /> * People who know vampires exist (easy to manufacture, hard to control in the long term)<br /> * The terminally ill<br /> * Military leaders (in the modern nights, NCOs with a command position, Officers)<br /> * Constables and Police<br /> * Natural philosophers/scientists<br /> * Poets<br /> * People who have outsmarted, outargued, defeated, or otherwise bested the vampire in some genuine way on at least one occasion, even if it is trivial. (No letting them win)<br /> * The dominant personality in a crowded room (very nasty -- requires going out to crowded rooms every night)<br /> * Widows and widowers<br /> * People whose children have died (can be manufactured but at a cost)<br /> * Sexual deviants (culture- and context-dependent, but not culturally <b><i>specific</i></b>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T10:53:27-07:00","id":1395626,"title":"","content":"My favourite Ventrue feeding type is amputees. <br /> If you can't find one, make one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T10:58:43-07:00","id":1395628,"title":"","content":"In general I think that feeding preferences are something that should be kept a secret and that inquiring about your guest\u2019s feeding preferences would be rude and suspicious at the very least.<br /> <br /> The way I think of feeding restrictions is that the Ventrue have high standards, they won\u2019t lower themselves to drink blood that is beneath them. I have sometimes thought that if I were a Ventrue, I would, like Penelope\u2019s character, only drink from women who I was attracted to since the act of blood drinking is a semi-sexual kind of act. I could imagine a racist Ventrue only being willing to drink from their own race, we have the traditional virgin (presumably non-virgins are impure) blood preference, a Jewish or Muslim Ventrue might select blood based on some interpretation of Kosher or Halal. I think that much rarer would be drinking blood based on some moral standard, such as only drinking the blood of criminals or animals - because in those cases the Ventrue limits himself to inferior blood which seems unfitting with the nature of the Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T12:29:33-07:00","id":1395644,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> But for real, people getting their arms and legs chopped off is gonna get noticed.<br /> <br /> \u201cFirst I cut off arms, then legs, then head...\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T12:44:50-07:00","id":1395652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395587-ventrue-feeding-preferences?p=1395644#post1395644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> But for real, people getting their arms and legs chopped off is gonna get noticed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, such extremes wouldn't be necessary. Just losing a finger would qualify one as an amputee. losing facial features can count one as an amputee. Hell, one could argue something as simple as a circumcision would be an amputation (but I wouldn't really want to play a ventrue who'd allow that kinda chicanery). It's very much an excellent feeding restriction in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T17:32:33-07:00","id":1395704,"title":"","content":"It's a block for me, it's always stopped me playing a Ventrue and I tend to switch it for something else in my chronicles unless I have any Ventrue player characters. But here are a few I've thought &quot;that might work&quot;:<br /> <br /> People the vampire has bested in a fair fight. (For a given value of 'fair' that the vampire holds to. One of the major <b>Dark Ages</b> SPCs, a knight commander, has something like this.)<br /> Smokers. (You can make anybody smoke, but that doesn't make them a 'smoker'.)<br /> People who have a specific kind of food, drink or drug in their system. (Which you can arrange, so let's make it something expensive or otherwise complicated.)<br /> Insomniacs. (Reasonably easy for vampires to find, but makes it difficult to be a Sandman.)<br /> A given star sign. (They were Embraced in the early 70s.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T18:49:45-07:00","id":1395720,"title":"","content":"Most feeding restrictions are variations of a theme. These themes are not necessarily exclusive, but can often be combined.<ul><li>Someone belonging to a group they like or belong to themselves.</li> <li>Someone belonging to a group they don't like or are enemies to their group.</li> <li>Someone that displays an attribute or follows an activity that is sexually attractive or a fetish to them.</li> <li>Someone displays an attribute or performs an activity that they consider a vice or which angers or repels them.</li> <li>Someone within a certain age category.</li> <li>Someone within a certain ethnicity.</li> <li>Someone who displays a certain physical feature.</li> <li>Someone who displays a certain personality or mental feature.</li> <li>Someone who occupies a certain occupation or performs a certain social role.</li> <li>Someone who arouses a certain emotion in them (fear, hate, love, disgust, jealousy, envy, admiration, etc.).</li> <li>Someone who is in a certain emotional state.</li> <li>Someone who fits an odd esoteric criteria (something that isn't obvious about them, but can be learned through study or interaction - their Zodiac sign, their name's numerological significance, their familial status).</li> <li>Someone who lives in a specific kind of place.</li> <li>Someone who suffers from a particular sickness, ailment, or disease</li> </ul>The above is not exhaustive, and I'm sure I've left out many potential themes, despite the above being fairly generic. But I found once you identify a theme, it is very easy to run a whole series of variations with that theme. You do that with enough themes, and you'll have lots of prey exclusions. <br /> <br /> In general, you can then group those themes into two major themes - people the vampire either approves of, or people the vampire does not approve of. In other words, they feed on only the best available to them, or they feed on people they won't miss.<br /> <br /> In terms of specifics, I've used the following for either PCs or NPCs I've created.<ul><li>Humans who are in good general health (no acute or chronic illnesses, morbidities, disorders, etc.)</li> <li>Humans who the vampire is sexually attracted to</li> <li>Humans who the vampire feels are social parasites and the world is better off without them</li> <li>Humans who are criminals or other predators of their fellow man</li> <li>Humans who are near death (dying from wounds/injury, or diagnosed with fatal disease)</li> <li>Humans who are close blood relations (descended from a common ancestor)</li> <li>Humans who fit a certain physical profile (over 5'4&quot; in height, natural hair color is not black, eyes not brown)</li> <li>Humans of a particular blood type (e.g. only blood type &quot;B&quot;, or &quot;not O+&quot;)</li> <li>Humans who have an extroverted personality/social butterfly</li> <li>Humans who are sexual virgins</li> <li>Humans who are sexually promiscuous (with an agreed upon definition between the ST and PC)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T19:00:55-07:00","id":1395721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nosimplehiway</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1395587-ventrue-feeding-preferences#post1395587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an ST, how do you decide which feeding preferences to approve for pcs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is really a question of fairness to the other PCs. How much do their clan weaknesses come into effect? You want your Ventrue PCs to not feel particularly favored or disfavored compared to the other PCs. There is an exception - some players may want to roleplay a particularly hard feeding restriction because they like the challenge or feel it makes for good roleplay, in which case you should indulge them while making sure the restriction is something that is viable throughout the entire chronicle.<br /> <br /> In general, I would want a Ventrue PC to have to work harder than the other PCs to find appropriate vessels, but not the extent it hijacks the game. That PC should still be able to feel he is able to interact with the plot and contribute to the coterie's success and have fun without fear his restriction will ruin things. Although again, if you run rotating stories that focus on one particular PC before going to the next, when it comes to the Ventrue's spotlight sessions, that may be something you concentrate on instead of other elements of that PC.<br /> <br /> I expect a feeding restriction to at least eliminate half the human population available to him, but anything more restrictive I typically leave up to the players to determine. For NPCs, I'm typically more restrictive, desiring a restriction that leaves at most a quarter of the human population, but still leaves them plenty enough to survive. If I choose a very restrictive feeding restriction (like the aforementioned Bobby Weatherbottom's) it is because I have a particular story in mind where I'm using that Ventrue as a showcase.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}